    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. Benefiting from a favorable matchup against Civale, **Gunnar Henderson** captures the optimal convergence of a #1 lineup spot, positive park factors, and a dynamic platoon advantage. He is joined in the elite tier by **Kyle Tucker** (75.90) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.04). Despite facing a high-caliber arm in Strider, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s upside remains undeniable due to his SP Skill adjusted projection, while **Jackson Merrill** thrives today thanks to a significant platoon edge and his elite ability to steal bases\u2014a crucial metric for our 5x5 Roto standing. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.10) also projects well, capitalizing on a weak matchup against Kochanowicz, where his xwOBA and SP Skill advantage overcome the minor dynamic platoon penalty.\n\nStrategic roster construction for this slate relies heavily on the \"Wind Out\" conditions and platoon stacking, which propelled **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (67.75) and **Andy Pages** (67.55) into high-confidence starts. **Sam Antonacci** (63.73) remains a pivot point; while facing Castillo is no small task, his projection is buoyed by favorable wind and an elite xwOBA profile that justifies his inclusion despite the tough opposition. Conversely, our most difficult decision involved **Miguel Vargas** (54.01). He narrowly missed the cut behind **Brady House** (54.45), whose dynamic platoon edge against Junk provided just enough of a statistical cushion to warrant the start over the bench options. \n\nOwners should exercise caution regarding the pending lineup statuses for **Drake Baldwin**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**. We have assumed optimal placement for these players, but any drop in their respective batting orders will necessitate a downward revision of their daily efficiency scores. Additionally, while **Josh Lowe** (57.15) holds a marginal start grade, his low spot in the order acts as a drag on his potential; he remains a start only due to the specific lack of better alternatives on the bench today. Monitor pre-game weather reports specifically for the games involving **Coby Mayo**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Heliot Ramos**, as the current \"Wind Out\" forecasts are primary drivers for their elevated projections.",
